  "question": {
    "text": "A ball is dropped vertically from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;above the ground. It hits the ground and bounces up vertically to a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Neglecting subsequent motion and air resistance, its velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> varies with height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> above the ground as",
    "image": null
  },
