  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the uniformly accelerated/decelcrated motion,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math></p><p>So. from this equation. we can say&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;paragraph is parabola.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/9a271acb-9ff1-4c78-bc96-8aba42a9ec7d-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 218px;\" /></p><p>Initially, velocity is downwards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;after collision, it reverses the direction with smaller magnitude and velocity is upwards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>So. graph (a) satisfies these conditions.</p><p>Also, When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;Velocity increases downwards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> velocity reverses its direction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
